Yes, but this C-code doesn't apply here. As the thread evolved it may
not have been that clear, but the program excerpt I posted (or Ralf's
posting) should make it obvious.
The factors are *NOT* calculated as 100 * (4/3) * (3/2)  rather it's
summed up by percentages of the original value, depending on charisma
and other factors. For example, you need a charisma less than 6 to get
to pay 200 for a base price 100 scroll; but that is a simple expression
100*2. With modifiers you won't get that round number; for example with
a charisma of 6 and a surcharge condition you will have to pay 199 (and
not 200), because it's incrementally added; 100+33=133, 133+66=199. The
first 33 is 33% of 100, the next 66 is 50% of the incremented value 133.
